Answer: For a matrix whose indexes range from 0 to n, the secondary diagonal satisfies: i + j = n For example, when n = 10: i = 0, j = 10 → 10 i = 1, j = 9 → 10 i = 2, j = 8 → 10 i = 3, j = 7 → 10 ... i = 10, j = 0 → 10 Therefore, the condition is:

```java
if (i + j == n) {
System.out.print("* ");
